//www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70084","state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","description":"View one of the most distinctive rock outcroppings on the district that overlooks the Rogue River watershed. Provides access to: Hanging Rock Trail #1113, a 0.25 mile long trail from trailhead that leads to the Pather Ridge Trail #1253 which accesses Wild Rogue Wilderness . Facilities No picnic table No fire pit No drinking water No toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out","forest":"Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest","cost":"free","feeDescription":"No fee","activityType":"Trailhead"},{"id":"usfs-ri-paradise-44.544_-116.952","name":"PARADISE","type":"campground","lat":44.544172,"lon":-116.95202,"source":"USFS","reservable":false,"amenities":["potable water","restrooms"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["USFS"],"state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","totalSites":15,"cost":"free","feeDescription":"No fees are required for this site","siteType":"CAMPGROUND"},{"id":"usfs-e0a72aeb2568d48f","name":"Paradise Campground","type":"campground","lat":44.543862,"lon":-116.95245,"source":"USFS","sourceId":"26949","reservable":false,"amenities":[],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service - Payette National Forest","sources":["USFS"],"feeDescription":"No fee charged for these sites.&nbsp;","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/payette/recarea/?recid=26949","state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","forest":"Willamette National Forest","description":"<p>Paradise Campground is indeed a campers paradise. Originally built by the Civilian Conservation Corps in the 1930s, it offers a rare opportunity to camp in the middle of a lush, old growth grove of Douglas fir and western red cedar while viewing the McKenzie River&#39;s famous white water.</p><p>A number of the 64 sites face the river, while many others are tucked into the scenic forest. Flush toilets are dispersed throughout the campground and parking spurs are paved. Educational programs ar","season":"May - October"},{"id":"usfs-paradise-campground-44.184_-122.090","name":"Paradise Campground","type":"dispersed","lat":44.184029,"lon":-122.090139,"source":"USFS","sourceId":"4380","reservable":false,"amenities":["restrooms","RV accessible"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["USFS"],"url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/willamette/recarea/?recid=4380","state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","description":"Paradise Campground is indeed a campers paradise. Originally built by the Civilian Conservation Corps in the 1930s, it offers a rare opportunity to camp in the middle of a lush, old growth grove of Douglas fir and western red cedar while viewing the McKenzie River's famous white water. A number of the 64 sites face the river, while many others are tucked into the scenic forest. Flush toilets are dispersed throughout the campground and parking spurs are paved. Educational programs are provided at","forest":"Willamette National Forest","cost":"$$","feeDescription":"Single Campsites - $30 per night Multiple Campsites - $60 per night Extra Vehicles - $10 per vehicle, per night Download the Recreation.gov mobile app prior to your trip so you can pay the overnight fee onsite with Scan and Pay .","season":"May - October","activityType":"Campground Camping"},{"id":"usfs-ri-paradise-campground-44.186_-122.096","name":"PARADISE CAMPGROUND","type":"campground","lat":44.18611,"lon":-122.09611,"source":"USFS","reservable":false,"amenities":["potable water","restrooms"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["USFS"],"state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","totalSites":355,"cost":"$$","season":"44687","elevation":1600,"feeDescription":"Overnight Use: Single Site: $29 per night Double Site $58 Additional Vehicle Fee: $10 per vehicle per day","siteType":"CAMPGROUND"},{"id":"merged-46e80847b51ed618","name":"Paradise Creek campground","type":"campground","lat":45.95,"lon":-121.936667,"source":"Recreation.gov","sourceId":"232862","reservable":true,"reservationUrl":"https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232862","amenities":["RV","Tent","Trailer"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["Recreation.gov","USFS"],"fee":25,"feeMax":45,"rating":4.6,"totalSites":41,"city":"Stevenson","season":"05/17/2024 - 09/22/2024","feeDescription":"Camping: Reservations stasrt on May 24th, 2024\\r\\n\\r\\n\\t\\r\\n\\t\\tSingle Site/$25\\r\\n\\t\\tMulti-Site/$45\\r\\n\\t\\r\\n\\t\\r\\n\\tExtra Vehicle:$8","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/giffordpinchot/recarea/?recid=31870","state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon"},{"id":"usfs-ri-paradise-creek-cg-45.950_-121.938","name":"PARADISE CREEK CG","type":"campground","lat":45.9502,"lon":-121.9378,"source":"USFS","reservable":false,"amenities":["potable water","restrooms"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["USFS"],"state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","totalSites":245,"cost":"$$","season":"46143","elevation":1600,"feeDescription":"Overnight Use: Single Site: $25 per night Double Site: $45 per night Additional Vehicle Fee: $8 per vehicle per night","siteType":"CAMPGROUND"},{"id":"usfs-paradise-day-use-area-44.184_-122.090","name":"Paradise Day Use Area","type":"campground","lat":44.184159,"lon":-122.090038,"source":"USFS","sourceId":"4381","reservable":false,"amenities":["RV accessible"],"managingAgency":"USDA Forest Service","sources":["USFS"],"url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/willamette/recarea/?recid=4381","state":"OR","stateName":"Oregon","description":"Paradise lives up to its name. Originally build by the Civilian Conservation Corps in the 1930s, it offers a rare opportunity to picnic in the middle of an old-growth grove while viewing McKenzie River's famous white water. The day use site is adjacent to Paradise Campground and offers picnicking, river access and an amphitheater.","forest":"Willamette National Forest","cost":"free","feeDescription":"No Fee","activityType":"Picnicking"},{"id":"recreation.gov-b6c61040417ebaf9","name":"PARADISE IN OREGON","type":"campground","lat":